  "units": "m",
  "description": "Interactive 3D figure for the laws of reflection, book page 215, topic 8.2.1, next to চিত্র ৮.০৩. A calm mountain lake is the setting: a snow mountain mirrored exactly in the water. The view then flies close to the point of incidence and looks down at the water from a three-quarter angle, as চিত্র ৮.০৩ does, and the figure builds one part at a time, each with a moment's glow and its book term: the ray XO, the point O, the perpendicular (অভিলম্ব), the upright plane with its foot on the water and its 90°, the reflected ray OX′, and the angles θi and θr. The student turns the plane round the normal by a handle on a circle on the water while the camera stays put (the reflected ray stays in it, the first law) and drags X (θr = θi live, the second law), with both laws word for word in the panel. The last step is 8.2.2, back on the whole lake: the mountain's image is crisp on still water and breaks into a shimmer on waves, and one magnifier shows why, with three parallel rays traced on a cross-section of the surface: parallel on a straight line, spread out (ব্যাপ্ত প্রতিফলন) on a wavy one, each ray obeying the law about its own normal. Five test questions. Offline, Bangla and English.",
